# Two separate reasons for this file, and only the first is about git:
#
#   - This folder is its own repository, so this is the only .gitignore that applies to it. It
#     used to sit inside the monorepo, whose root rules covered all of this; they do not travel
#     with the folder.
#   - Steam does not read .gitignore at all. SteamUGC.SetItemContent takes the junction's target
#     directory as it stands on disk, with no filtering, so anything sitting in the published
#     folder is published. That is what `Mod/` is for: the junction points there, and everything
#     else in this folder - Art/, Source/, the docs, this file - stays out of reach by
#     construction.

# Build intermediates. Source/Directory.Build.props already sends them to ../.build/, so the
# two entries below are belt and braces against a build run with the props file bypassed - which
# would drop a 6 MB publicised Assembly-CSharp.dll inside the mod.
.build/
Source/obj/
Source/bin/

# Claude Code session state and local settings, never shared.
.claude/

# Showcase notes: French working notes, deleted once Preview.png and ModIcon.png are done.
PROMPT_*.md

# Development environments.
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.csproj.user

# System.
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
